Now I have everything I need. Here's my analysis and recommendations:

---

## Current AI Implementation Analysis

### What's Already Good
The current `vision.ts` prompt is quite comprehensive:
- Asks for exact product names, model numbers, brands
- Requests specific colorways and materials
- Generates optimized search queries
- Has detailed identification tips for different categories
- Uses GPT-4o with high detail vision

### Current Limitations

1. **Missing Categories**: The prompt doesn't explicitly mention some items:
   - Swimwear, activewear, loungewear
   - Ties, pocket squares, cufflinks
   - Glasses (prescription), hair accessories
   - Socks, underwear (when visible)
   - Phone cases, wallets, keychains

2. **Search Query Optimization for Awin**: The `searchQuery` is generic - not optimized for your specific Awin feed which has:
   - Specific merchants (Cerqular, Fashiontamers, Babubas, etc.)
   - Product names in format: "Brand Name Product Type - Color"
   - Fashion attributes in description: "Brand: X, Type: Y, Model: Z, Color: W"

3. **Missing Attributes** that could improve matching:
   - Gender (men's/women's/unisex)
   - Size indicators (if visible)
   - Season/collection
   - Style (casual, formal, sporty, streetwear)
   - Fit (slim, regular, oversized)
   - Pattern (solid, striped, plaid, floral)

4. **Single Image Limitation**: Currently processes one image, could benefit from multiple angles

---

## Recommended Enhancements

### 1. Enhanced Detection Interface
```typescript
export interface DetectedProduct {
  // Current fields
  name: string;
  exactModel: string | null;
  brand: string | null;
  category: string;
  color: string;
  material: string | null;
  description: string;
  confidence: number;
  isHighlighted: boolean;
  searchQuery: string;

  // NEW fields for better matching
  gender: "men" | "women" | "unisex" | "kids" | null;
  style: string | null;        // e.g., "casual", "formal", "athletic", "streetwear"
  pattern: string | null;      // e.g., "solid", "striped", "checkered", "floral"
  fit: string | null;          // e.g., "slim", "regular", "oversized", "cropped"
  season: string | null;       // e.g., "SS24", "FW23", "all-season"
  subCategory: string | null;  // e.g., "running shoes", "midi dress", "crossbody bag"

  // Multiple search query variants
  searchQueries: {
    specific: string;    // "Nike Air Force 1 07 Low Triple White Men's"
    generic: string;     // "white leather sneakers men"
    brandFocused: string; // "Nike white sneakers low top"
  };

  // Visual attributes for verification
  visualAttributes: {
    primaryColors: string[];     // ["white", "black"]
    accentColors: string[];      // ["red"]
    logoVisible: boolean;
    logoPlacement: string | null; // "chest", "heel", "front"
    distinctiveFeatures: string[]; // ["perforated toe", "gum sole"]
  };
}
```

### 2. Expanded Categories
Add more granular categories and sub-categories:

```typescript
// Main categories (keep existing)
type ProductCategory = "top" | "bottom" | "dress" | "outerwear" | "shoes" | "accessory" | "bag" | "jewelry" | "swimwear" | "activewear" | "other";

// Sub-categories for better search
const SUB_CATEGORIES = {
  top: ["t-shirt", "polo", "shirt", "blouse", "sweater", "hoodie", "cardigan", "tank top", "crop top", "tunic"],
  bottom: ["jeans", "chinos", "trousers", "shorts", "leggings", "joggers", "cargo pants", "wide-leg pants"],
  dress: ["mini dress", "midi dress", "maxi dress", "bodycon", "shift dress", "wrap dress", "shirt dress"],
  outerwear: ["jacket", "coat", "blazer", "vest", "parka", "windbreaker", "bomber", "denim jacket", "leather jacket"],
  shoes: ["sneakers", "running shoes", "boots", "ankle boots", "loafers", "oxfords", "sandals", "heels", "flats", "slides"],
  accessory: ["hat", "cap", "beanie", "sunglasses", "belt", "scarf", "tie", "watch", "wallet", "gloves"],
  bag: ["backpack", "tote", "crossbody", "clutch", "shoulder bag", "messenger", "duffel", "fanny pack"],
  jewelry: ["necklace", "bracelet", "earrings", "ring", "anklet", "brooch", "cufflinks"],
  swimwear: ["bikini", "one-piece", "swim trunks", "cover-up", "rash guard"],
  activewear: ["sports bra", "yoga pants", "running shorts", "tank", "track jacket"]
};
```

### 3. Enhanced Prompt
Key improvements to the AI prompt:

```
1. EXPLICITLY request ALL visible items (even partially visible)
2. Add gender detection
3. Add style/occasion classification
4. Add pattern recognition
5. Generate MULTIPLE search query variants
6. Request distinctive visual features for verification
7. Better handling of unknown brands (describe what you see)
```

### 4. Search Query Strategy for Awin
Since your Awin feed has specific formats, generate queries optimized for it:

```typescript
// Current Awin product names look like:
// "Adidas Taekwondo Mei W Sftm Black Sneakers"
// "NIKE Womens Grey Hoodie Dress Cotton Sleeveless"

// So searchQuery should match this pattern:
// "{Brand} {Gender indicator} {Color} {Product Type} {Material/Style}"
```

### 5. Post-Processing Improvements
Add a verification step that compares AI detection with Awin results:

```typescript
// Score Awin products against AI-detected attributes
function scoreAwinMatch(awinProduct: AwinProduct, detected: DetectedProduct): number {
  let score = 0;

  // Brand match in description
  if (detected.brand && awinProduct.description.toLowerCase().includes(detected.brand.toLowerCase())) {
    score += 10;
  }

  // Color match
  if (detected.visualAttributes.primaryColors.some(c => 
    awinProduct.product_name.toLowerCase().includes(c) ||
    awinProduct.description.toLowerCase().includes(c)
  )) {
    score += 5;
  }

  // Category/type match
  if (awinProduct.category_name.toLowerCase().includes(detected.subCategory)) {
    score += 5;
  }

  // Gender match
  if (detected.gender && awinProduct.product_name.toLowerCase().includes(detected.gender)) {
    score += 3;
  }

  return score;
}
```

